Reusing a ``PyLinter`` instance to check files several times no longer
accumulates the messages and statistics of previous runs: the score, the
reports and the exit status now only describe the files and messages of the
current run.

Pylint now exits with the usage error code (``32``) when every input file was
ignored or excluded and no file could actually be checked, instead of returning
``0`` like a successful run without any message.
